OLS estimates with respondent-clustered standard errors in parentheses. Binary outcomes ($A$, $S^{\Sexpr{selection_window_seconds}}$) are in percentage points. Covariates are centered at the analytical-sample mean and interacted with condition, so the condition rows are the regression-adjusted contrasts of Table~\ref{tab:primary} and the covariate rows are slopes in \armB; the eight covariate-by-condition interactions are estimated but not shown. The main estimates, Equation~\eqref{eq:dim}, contain only the condition indicators and are reported in Table~\ref{tab:primary}. Task-position indicators are omitted because every respondent completes all \Sexpr{n_main_tasks} tasks, which makes them orthogonal to all regressors.
